  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The rate constants for decomposition of acetaldehyde have been measured over the temperature range <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The data has been analysed by plotting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>lnk</mi></math> vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> graph. The value of activation energy for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Nearest integer) (Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0103_0b9e016b1a60.png\" style=\"width: 214px; height: 200px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "154",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Ae</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mrow><mi>RT</mi></mfrac></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>lnk</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>lnA</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mi>RT</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>lnk</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>lnA</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Slope&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>153</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>735</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>154</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>KJ</mi></math></p>"
